  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes: 176 tests, 0 failed. I didn't commit anything.\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):** I added `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release`. Availability and expiry use only the store's `clock`. `removeItem` now throws `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` when the quantity is more than what is available, not just more than physical stock.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`. `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the status codes you listed.\n- **Tests (`test/reservations.test.js`):** The new tests cover the store behaviours, including expiry exactly at creation time plus `ttlMs`, and the API flows and error codes.\n\n- **`confirm` return value:** I made `confirm` return `{sku, stock}` so the API can use it directly.\n- **`ttlMs` not validated:** The spec didn't mention it, so I left it unchecked.\n- **Expired reservations stay in memory:** They aren't purged. That is what lets `confirm` tell expired from not found, but the map grows over time.",
